<title>CHILE: Madeco sees revenues rising.</title>
<headline>Madeco sees revenues rising.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manufacturas de Cobre SA, or Madeco, expects revenues this year to climb to $900 million from $630 million in 1996 and $598 million in 1995, General Manager Carlos Vicuna said.</p>
<p>The Chilean copper and aluminum products firm made its 1997 estimates on the basis of an expected $1 average price per pound for copper, Vicuna said.</p>
<p>The company's growth in Chile this year will be roughly at the same rate as in 1996, he told a news conference.</p>
<p>Higher revenues will come mainly from its recently-acquired Ficap wire unit in Brazil and expected stronger sales for Madeco's line of building materials in Argentina, said Vicuna.</p>
<p>--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
